# Distant painted cloud polar concept v01

Built-in image_gen. Source grayscale artwork, not channel-packed runtime data. Center represents zenith; outer rim represents horizon. Layout visually reviewed; precise dome projection and ground-view appearance remain to be validated in-engine. Preserve independent Coverage and Shade when preparing runtime assets; do not equate dark painted shading with transparency.

## Prompt

Use case: stylized-concept. Create a production concept of a POLAR UV CLOUD TEXTURE, square canvas, circular upper-sky hemisphere mapped as azimuthal equidistant polar UV: exact center = zenith, outer circular perimeter = horizon, angle around center = azimuth, radius increases toward horizon. This is NOT a normal landscape panorama and NOT a decorative wreath. Attached images are STYLE REFERENCES: match their grayscale hand-painted gouache clouds, broad layered gray strokes, charcoal shading, restrained highlights, selective soft and broken edges. Strict grayscale, opaque pure black sky/background including outside the circular footprint. No labels, guides, rings, grid, text, moon, sun, stars or landscape. CRITICAL SCALE: these clouds are FAR AWAY as seen by a ground-level game character. No gigantic foreground clouds, no mass occupying the zenith. Keep the central 50 percent of the circle radius almost empty; concentrate small and medium distant clouds mainly from 65 to 95 percent radius, with plenty of uneven gaps. Roughly 10-14 distinct asymmetrical cloud groupings around the horizon and 3-5 sparse thin wisps a little inward. Only 2 modest taller cloud groups, still small in apparent angular size. Cloud bases face radially OUTWARD toward the horizon; cloud crowns rise radially INWARD toward the center. Rotate each cloud grouping with its azimuth, as proper polar-mapped sky artwork: bottom sector bases downward and crowns upward, top sector bases upward and crowns downward, left sector bases leftward and crowns rightward, right sector bases rightward and crowns leftward. Clouds nearer the outer edge are progressively smaller and thinner. Maintain individual silhouettes and dark painted interior shade like the references. Avoid evenly repeated stamps or a solid circular cloud wall. Keep all actual cloud pixels inside the circular footprint and a small black canvas border. High resolution square texture, clean soft distant-cloud composition, quiet open overhead sky. Grayscale SHADE concept source only, not false-color channel packing.
